{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpnRfaC7rsiU1sb6nMiq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In Vitest 5, `vitest list` **parses test files statically by default** instead of running them. It reads each file's source, builds a syntax tree, and looks for calls like `describe`, `test`/`it`, and modifiers such as `.skip`, `.only`, and `.each`. From those calls it reconstructs the suite and test hierarchy and names without importing the file or running any of its code.\n\nThe tradeoff is that static analysis only sees what is written literally in the source. Tests created at runtime may not be listed accurately, such as names built in loops, tests generated from imported data, or tests created through wrapper helpers.\n\nEarlier versions of Vitest collected tests by actually importing the files. That ran their top-level code but not the test bodies.\n\n(Source: Vitest 5.0.0 release notes, https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases/tag/v5.0.0)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3476,"cache_read_input_tokens":544,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3476},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9247599f-4c69-49a0-a408-0af0a1d2a497","uuid":"f19e4d81-aa7c-49ab-b01a-af2e2a988be0","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:39:09.872Z","request_id":"req_011CfpnRfJZwkjPZEHhdyrhi"}
